{"title":"2004 AIME II Problems/Problem 7","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solutions\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solutions</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_1_(Synthetic)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1 (Synthetic)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(analytic)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (analytic)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Coordinate_Bashing)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Coordinate Bashing)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_4_(Trig)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4 (Trig)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Solution_5_(Fast,_Pythagorean)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5 (Fast, Pythagorean)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Solution_6(fast_as_wind[rufeng])\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 6(fast as wind[rufeng])</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Solution_7_(Similar_to_solution_5,_more_in_depth)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 7 (Similar to solution 5, more in depth)</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> is a rectangular sheet of paper that has been folded so that corner <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> is matched with point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/7/4c71f19552a05ee5e2b31e94aff3fb986884bf31.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B&#39;$\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> on edge <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/8/f386fc0035258fe8780a97b973f9ea93679abf16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD.$\" width=\"32\" height=\"13\" /> The crease is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/3/40396601982527dbcfbddf5f8fa83b1cb3f09ed1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EF,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"30\" height=\"16\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/c/79c918bfa9b7b699552d7779d1de346b73d75010.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD.$\" width=\"33\" height=\"12\" /> The dimensions <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/b/beb85d6f9eba35e2469c1ed8c2c78eccf01079c2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AE=8, BE=17,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"145\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/c/dec4947ded2f2d94fcd4ef6b4254686e3798cfd5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CF=3$\" width=\"61\" height=\"12\" /> are given. The perimeter of rectangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/1/271cdd78c4c10cde94410584ce7282874413cb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m/n,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"40\" height=\"18\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> are relatively prime positive integers. Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/b/5db26f75f6218a382840f0ed34f5d36bcff61d33.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+n.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"56\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/2/8320d3082101e1e3a6a8d6b283794ffbdc9cf7b5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] size(200); defaultpen(linewidth(0.7)+fontsize(10)); pair A=origin, B=(25,0), C=(25,70/3), D=(0,70/3), E=(8,0), F=(22,70/3), Bp=reflect(E,F)*B, Cp=reflect(E,F)*C; draw(F--D--A--E); draw(E--B--C--F, linetype(&quot;4 4&quot;)); filldraw(E--F--Cp--Bp--cycle, white, black); pair point=( 12.5, 35/3 ); label(&quot;$A$&quot;, A, dir(point--A)); label(&quot;$B$&quot;, B, dir(point--B)); label(&quot;$C$&quot;, C, dir(point--C)); label(&quot;$D$&quot;, D, dir(point--D)); label(&quot;$E$&quot;, E, dir(point--E)); label(&quot;$F$&quot;, F, dir(point--F)); label(&quot;$B^\\prime$&quot;, Bp, dir(point--Bp)); label(&quot;$C^\\prime$&quot;, Cp, dir(point--Cp));[/asy]\" width=\"332\" height=\"335\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solutions\">Solutions</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solutions\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span id=\"Solution_1_.28Synthetic.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1_(Synthetic)\">Solution 1 (Synthetic)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1 (Synthetic)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/4/e8476256c3a6cf7cf8b766055c9c035fb86817da.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] pointpen = black; pathpen = black +linewidth(0.7); pair A=(0,0),B=(0,25),C=(70/3,25),D=(70/3,0),E=(0,8),F=(70/3,22),G=(15,0); D(MP(&quot;A&quot;,A)--MP(&quot;B&quot;,B,N)--MP(&quot;C&quot;,C,N)--MP(&quot;D&quot;,D)--cycle); D(MP(&quot;E&quot;,E,W)--MP(&quot;F&quot;,F,(1,0))); D(B--G); D(E--MP(&quot;B&#39;&quot;,G)--F--B,dashed); MP(&quot;8&quot;,(A+E)/2,W);MP(&quot;17&quot;,(B+E)/2,W);MP(&quot;22&quot;,(D+F)/2,(1,0)); [/asy]\" width=\"248\" height=\"252\" /></center>\n<p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/2/c128243ea8125d0bb007b8132dcfa44461df73a7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EF$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> is the perpendicular bisector of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/0/2e0e06feaa3c61ff1386e726362f646529472c84.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{BB&#39;}$\" width=\"34\" height=\"15\" />, it follows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/3/48324eed039058dd39949df5f3337956776b91fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BE = B&#39;E$\" width=\"87\" height=\"14\" /> (by SAS). By the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Pythagorean_Theorem\" title=\"Pythagorean Theorem\">Pythagorean Theorem</a>, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/4/0e47df4762799c54ca1de4411be72aa406f446fd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB&#39; = 15$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"74\" height=\"14\" />. Similarly, from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/9/80909ef1a4fa3f52ef080eed05ddea3c26c1a255.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BF = B&#39;F$\" width=\"86\" height=\"14\" />, we have\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/d/b2d97b2acb8c98b9c9ff9cb420b2e92509542ed2.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} BC^2 + CF^2 = B&#39;D^2 + DF^2 &amp;\\Longrightarrow BC^2 + 9 = (BC - 15)^2 + 484 \\\\ BC  &amp;= \\frac{70}{3} \\end{align*}\" width=\"491\" height=\"64\" />\nThus the perimeter of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/f/affbd1ee79f1844e5136bb9619728f8118aae4a1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\left(25 + \\frac{70}{3}\\right) = \\frac{290}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"158\" height=\"45\" />, and our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/3/dc3a708b6b9723ed69c63d382af57e025ddeb7b4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+n=\\boxed{293}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"112\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<h3><span id=\"Solution_2_.28analytic.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(analytic)\">Solution 2 (analytic)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (analytic)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/a/7ca7e96dbc41b338256b4d9ee0a09468568bcee4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A = (0,0), B=(0,25)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"173\" height=\"18\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/9/30959954a5c36ac758f02c4ace28a0d57603ab8f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E = (0,8)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"77\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/c/a3c5ce794ece324e4ca36ee596f3ea013b3111df.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F = (l,22)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"86\" height=\"20\" />, and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/e/d6e60a394a7cbffc2d7ba40a83228cca9a3a30e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$l = AD$\" width=\"58\" height=\"13\" /> be the length of the rectangle. The <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Slope\" title=\"Slope\">slope</a> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/2/c128243ea8125d0bb007b8132dcfa44461df73a7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EF$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/8/bc834fefa7e24e8dd2433e82e03aec4704d29d8e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{14}{l}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"20\" height=\"37\" /> and so the equation of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/2/c128243ea8125d0bb007b8132dcfa44461df73a7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EF$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/c/a3cedb27173dfb40997d886884739b512a8fd590.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y -8 = \\frac{14}{l}x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"100\" height=\"38\" />. We know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/2/c128243ea8125d0bb007b8132dcfa44461df73a7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EF$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> is perpendicular to and bisects <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/a/c2ae0e30605dc87c83aecb3f588afa7129bee6aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BB&#39;$\" width=\"33\" height=\"14\" />. The slope of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/a/c2ae0e30605dc87c83aecb3f588afa7129bee6aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BB&#39;$\" width=\"33\" height=\"14\" /> is thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/e/dbe1b4d571d7d813a43a53473d9d54331207fdbc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{-l}{14}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"22\" height=\"38\" />, and so the equation of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/a/c2ae0e30605dc87c83aecb3f588afa7129bee6aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BB&#39;$\" width=\"33\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/f/5af7fd01b5d1c4c6e9b90d4007138b9de1925325.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y -25 = \\frac{-l}{14}x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"108\" height=\"38\" />. Let the point of intersection of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/1/84108076f29b81fcab6c1cb7d50f7ec2e30395a7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EF, BB&#39;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"71\" height=\"19\" /> be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/2/6e28ce12d49d39f160d5a0ef54077fc98e4b9d2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$G$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. Then the y-coordinate of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/2/6e28ce12d49d39f160d5a0ef54077fc98e4b9d2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$G$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/7/2d74e82f3b7ff8814639fa300e287c601edf9af4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{25}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"24\" height=\"38\" />, so\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/3/3e306365754996ca2d278072fff5c3a1710331f4.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} \\frac{14}{l}x &amp;= y-8 = \\frac{9}{2}\\\\ \\frac{-l}{14}x &amp;= y-25 = -\\frac{25}{2}\\\\ \\end{align*}\" width=\"165\" height=\"82\" />\nDividing the two equations yields\n</p>\n<center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/8/7e8ae577a847b2f8283ffcb1b85a61f570702b67.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$l^2 = \\frac{25 \\cdot 14^2}{9} \\Longrightarrow l = \\frac{70}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"188\" height=\"39\" /></center>\n<p>The answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/5/6956da675ee181a23acb94c34c33d8e341b8e6ec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{293}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"39\" height=\"23\" /> as above.\n</p>\n<h3><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Coordinate_Bashing.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Coordinate_Bashing)\">Solution 3 (Coordinate Bashing)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Coordinate Bashing)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Firstly, observe that if we are given that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/8/8982a7982c7df8159c047c172a2b90e531ee3865.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AE=8$\" width=\"61\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/4/064672d46283eb6b0bd9c00e14b84ebdecb749af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BE=17$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"71\" height=\"13\" />, the length of the triangle is given and the height depends solely on the length of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/d/07d29465728e92952374a857beaee91665d8dbd9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CF$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" />. Let Point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/3/7b3d9b8d04d50e4d2615681c9fc75b55592a7e43.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A = (0,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"76\" height=\"18\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/8/8982a7982c7df8159c047c172a2b90e531ee3865.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AE=8$\" width=\"61\" height=\"13\" />, point E is at (8,0). Next, point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> is at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/3/d63d48ada3e2af8a43938f8f7e05c012ab200a63.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(25,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"48\" height=\"18\" /> since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/4/064672d46283eb6b0bd9c00e14b84ebdecb749af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BE=17$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"71\" height=\"13\" /> and point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/7/4c71f19552a05ee5e2b31e94aff3fb986884bf31.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B&#39;$\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> is at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/a/47a83b9725f6881f9ad8fd7721b393e6b7f26d36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(0,15)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"47\" height=\"18\" /> since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/4/2944baa0300c92737e69530158523f7a98927507.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BE=AE$\" width=\"81\" height=\"13\" /> by symmetry. Draw line segment <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/a/c2ae0e30605dc87c83aecb3f588afa7129bee6aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BB&#39;$\" width=\"33\" height=\"14\" />. Notice that this is perpendicular to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/2/c128243ea8125d0bb007b8132dcfa44461df73a7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EF$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> by symmetry. Next, find the slope of EB, which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/7/4c7474650f4a0de28293ffb943a480a50d84ff7f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{15}{25}=\\frac{3}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"58\" height=\"37\" />. Then, the slope of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/2/c128243ea8125d0bb007b8132dcfa44461df73a7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EF$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> is -<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/e/9ae6ca439f90be5b87b92cab8cfd6ea9e3f23475.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{5}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"11\" height=\"37\" />. \n</p><p>Line EF can be written as y=<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/3/0f3eceb06bb906a08fd25171c2a1e9d344912ff7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-\\frac{5}{3}x+b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"68\" height=\"37\" />. Plug in the point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/3/37338b3604eb55e9193f4b1fb1f74e9843ad6666.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(8,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />, and we get the equation of EF to be y=<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/6/ab65bdab3bc29d215965aebf9dc137dd0ff84be8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$_\\frac{5}{3}x+\\frac{40}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"67\" height=\"38\" />. Since the length of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />=25, a point on line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/2/c128243ea8125d0bb007b8132dcfa44461df73a7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EF$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> lies on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/e/27e525b776c49bbe7d0ae66cfc7ab8f58f40624e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/a/aeaea97306538142814b711e8599748c958aa9fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=25-3=22$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"128\" height=\"15\" />. Plug in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/e/a4e56fbd39d7ceba5113524e3ed5ccdf7f36c9dc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=22$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"55\" height=\"14\" /> into our equation to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/0/ba0aafdea88e752708272f9cc918ff564bf8c435.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=-\\frac{70}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"68\" height=\"37\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/5/1e5fcbdc93dcefc4653dca3dd1d7f37447290468.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|y|=BC=\\frac{70}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"117\" height=\"37\" />. Therefore, our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/3/5131d9b6d9e0ff010e1ea099dea8638d57891802.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2(AB+BC)=2\\left(25+\\frac{70}{3}\\right)=2\\left(\\frac{145}{3}\\right)=\\frac{290}{3}= \\boxed{293}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"440\" height=\"43\" />.\n</p>\n<h3><span id=\"Solution_4_.28Trig.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4_(Trig)\">Solution 4 (Trig)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4 (Trig)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Firstly, note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/7/277344d96a923771ba1e96ca55d9ef20068cb9dc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B&#39;E=BE=17$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"129\" height=\"14\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/b/92b98d2aa73dc2ffc424a363fbd09370abf140bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB&#39;=\\sqrt{17^2-8^2}=15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"178\" height=\"18\" />. Then let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/e/94e8c4cb82a182464c40059499635e90af7f02bb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BEF=\\angle B&#39;EF=\\theta$\" width=\"174\" height=\"14\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/f/30f1d3adaafa52cd47d6a471921a3ef01d876cc8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle B&#39;EA = \\pi-2\\theta$\" width=\"135\" height=\"14\" />. Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/a/81a13588c75e24396ff63b93ea6e3b9dae1731cd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan(\\pi-2\\theta)=\\frac{15}{8}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"136\" height=\"37\" />, or \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/3/ea325dc22e7eefaf7cf9e39fc1681b7955e69778.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{2\\tan(\\theta)}{\\tan^2(\\theta)-1}=\\frac{15}{8}\\]\" width=\"135\" height=\"43\" /> using supplementary and double angle identities. Multiplying though and factoring yields \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/6/056597a6c8c8e02e0e65ea63d863ea397efa0cee.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(3\\tan(\\theta)-5)(5\\tan(\\theta)+3)=0\\]\" width=\"245\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>It is clear from the problem setup that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/a/7bafb18f0bfa719c4d082e1ea4c69da530ed58e4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0&lt;\\theta&lt;\\frac\\pi2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"80\" height=\"33\" />, so the correct value is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/9/859c193295cfa26f9e3c62f6685c3de19ed7f49c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan(\\theta)=\\frac53$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"85\" height=\"37\" />. Next, extend rays <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96a9c84a8c83e9a3467d061288a185c7de66d5a8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overrightarrow{BC}$\" width=\"28\" height=\"22\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/e/0fe3a8fa8076f20518f17dbe0af260f894777578.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overrightarrow{EF}$\" width=\"28\" height=\"22\" /> to intersect at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/7/9b798193cb94562989018728e1151587c618655b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C&#39;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"16\" />. Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/3/7c338033944ca7833b66027424afa1004e7f2599.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan(\\theta)=\\frac{BC&#39;}{17}=\\frac53$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"147\" height=\"38\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/f/84f3b18dd42cd2215b424d4a56f856f4a4e5355c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC&#39;=\\frac{85}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"82\" height=\"38\" />. By similar triangles, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/9/6394b98341ba6834d2ba4ff59b416720a2deb882.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CC&#39;=\\frac{3}{17}BC&#39;=\\frac{15}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"158\" height=\"38\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/a/c5aac4c02c89374c6b544f70fd2a5d1204af68a1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC=\\frac{70}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"73\" height=\"37\" />. The perimeter is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/e/47ed48bbde75600271d680c6a447e36fbc0e8088.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{140}{3}+50=\\frac{290}{3}\\Longrightarrow \\boxed{293}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"205\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p>An even faster way to finish is, to draw a line segment <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/d/53df72bce4ba938083684a5fc64dd68afc556fec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$FF&#39;$\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/7/6d794967bd855edced950369620307257fee99f8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F&#39;$\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> is a point on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/b/4bbe91133fdaa92f3e58b137fdb4db178296da61.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EB$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/d/53df72bce4ba938083684a5fc64dd68afc556fec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$FF&#39;$\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> is perpendicular to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/b/4bbe91133fdaa92f3e58b137fdb4db178296da61.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EB$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" />. This makes right triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/1/591e8477853053878fb66d91c752aefa0370356a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$FF&#39;E$\" width=\"47\" height=\"14\" />, Also, note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/7/b57dec9e683db67147925a1be7c87f699d8d5790.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F&#39;B$\" width=\"33\" height=\"14\" /> has length of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> (draw the diagram out, and note the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/7/48761b2a1793872b95ed8fec8efd4b415decc699.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F&#39;B =FC$\" width=\"86\" height=\"14\" />). From here, through <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/f/39fb554b09597261fef1c0d448c929d7c4891fae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan \\theta = \\frac{5}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"74\" height=\"37\" />, we can note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/b/88b77b802e9e13d89268377b12a516bb669ecb34.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{FF&#39;}{EF&#39;} = \\frac{5}{3} \\implies \\frac{FF&#39;}{14} = \\frac{5}{3} \\implies FF&#39; = \\frac{70}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"326\" height=\"38\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/d/53df72bce4ba938083684a5fc64dd68afc556fec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$FF&#39;$\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> is parallel and congrurent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/3/3e3a4ec0df571e719bd3f1d7e00bf71fc55ba2b9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CB$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/5/bc56862b1fdb71204894da278e42ef75de73a40b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />, and hence we can use this to calculate the perimeter. The perimeter is simply <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/8/498b27a5c42addac0bb49ed540438e6e0feb7723.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{70}{3} + \\frac{70}{3} + 25 + 25 = \\frac{290}{3} \\Longrightarrow \\boxed{293}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"281\" height=\"37\" />\n</p>\n<h3><span id=\"Solution_5_.28Fast.2C_Pythagorean.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5_(Fast,_Pythagorean)\">Solution 5 (Fast, Pythagorean)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5 (Fast, Pythagorean)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Use the prepared diagram for this solution.\n</p><p>Call the intersection of DF and B'C' G. AB'E is an 8-15-17 right triangle, and so are B'DG and C'FG. Since C'F is 3, then using the properties of similar triangles GF is 51/8. DF is 22, so DG is 125/8. Finally, DB can to calculated to be 25/3.\nAdd all the sides together to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/5/6956da675ee181a23acb94c34c33d8e341b8e6ec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{293}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"39\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p><p>-jackshi2006\n</p>\n<h3><span id=\"Solution_6.28fast_as_wind.5Brufeng.5D.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_6(fast_as_wind[rufeng])\">Solution 6(fast as wind[rufeng])</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 6(fast as wind[rufeng])\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Call the intersection of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/e/6aeaf3b3ed66bc4256b58d8123fbf178f31df9a7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B&#39;C&#39;$\" width=\"37\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/2/c128243ea8125d0bb007b8132dcfa44461df73a7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EF$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/2/6e28ce12d49d39f160d5a0ef54077fc98e4b9d2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$G$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/b/07bd528cf164713b966a36301868e501c28e517d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$FCBE$\" width=\"57\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/b/84b478ecd4b154853caa062aad42f1d13f6bd92e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$FC&#39;B&#39;E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"69\" height=\"16\" /> are congruent, we know that the three lines intersect.\nWe already know <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> so we just need to find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/3/3e3a4ec0df571e719bd3f1d7e00bf71fc55ba2b9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CB$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" />, call it <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />. Drop an altitude from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> and call it <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/9/b1902d279ba37d60bdce4e0e987b7cd19d48974e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$H$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/e/d7e32604c2dc1a35f8ed0ee9fc2ae728b723bb4a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EH=EB-FC=14$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"177\" height=\"13\" />. Using Pythagorean Theorem, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/8/2785f75fdd07fd7136d56a07d378e2bd0b6691f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EF=\\sqrt{x^2+14^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"134\" height=\"18\" />. Triangles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/f/4df8099148338e39565d6aa814f9749b9dc56782.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EFH$\" width=\"45\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/8/2f8c0dbda46ca48178fe91444c2f80f692db676c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EGB$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" /> are similar (AA), so we get\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/4/034b62015b7898117a838ac328c165e8e4303438.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{HF}{BG}=\\frac{EH}{EB}\\]\" width=\"90\" height=\"37\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/c/54c99548b19e5c9e073012d997f49f227a95d75c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{x}{x+GC}=\\frac{14}{17}\\]\" width=\"108\" height=\"38\" />\nSimplify and we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/9/009b0282a6a196f9d87dd03e174a3facf2345362.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$GC=\\frac{3x}{14}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"74\" height=\"38\" />. \n</p><p>We find the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/b/07bd528cf164713b966a36301868e501c28e517d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$FCBE$\" width=\"57\" height=\"12\" /> by using the fact that it is a trapezoid. \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/8/6288b844ddb19c5f159c6248327b114bcccd5319.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[FCBE]=\\frac{(3+17)x}{2}=10x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"222\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>A different way to find the area:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/a/91a4fb9a63f01e526d8789cb950ad058f0e8e7ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[FCBE]=\\frac{1}{2} EG\\cdot($\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"153\" height=\"37\" />height of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/8/2f8c0dbda46ca48178fe91444c2f80f692db676c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EGB$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/7/927d4689159fbeb80f7b468ca9ae96b48e926312.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EG$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" /> as base<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/8/838e7b7d49cc0de14d3f601a60d4472670dce6c3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$)-[FGC]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"80\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/4/81496e01bdcfe5c58e5dce3b6e3bd639bb9161f2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$GBE$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/1/7212147b3bc3d386e886fe7bf54cc12796f63edc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$G&#39;B&#39;E$\" width=\"52\" height=\"14\" /> are congruent(SAS), their height from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/7/927d4689159fbeb80f7b468ca9ae96b48e926312.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EG$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" /> is the same. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/1/cc14e776420e1dfa3468e80f3a7e393e5dc156e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B&#39;B=\\sqrt{AB&#39;^2+AB^2}=5\\sqrt{34}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"238\" height=\"19\" />.\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/2/b726243f1e925e4289551e711d7b503ece65aa93.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EG=\\sqrt{EB^2+BG^2}=\\sqrt{(\\frac{17x}{14})^2+17^2}=17\\sqrt{\\frac{x^2}{196}+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -14px\" width=\"430\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/f/39f897fdd22ad1c63932ac0e2fd9dd19eb0f9f49.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[[FCBE]=\\frac{1}{2} \\cdot 17 \\cdot \\sqrt{\\frac{x^2}{196}+1} \\cdot \\frac{5\\sqrt{34}}{2}-\\frac{9x}{28}\\]\" width=\"331\" height=\"43\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/4/784d4c06e4e5343d3df1bbcefbc991340bdc2664.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[280x+9x=7\\cdot 5 \\cdot \\sqrt{34} \\cdot 17 \\cdot \\sqrt{\\frac{x^2}{196}+1}\\]\" width=\"306\" height=\"43\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/e/5fe680ce1e8b0708a97f4003c024a758d714820d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[17^4 x^2=49 \\cdot 25 \\cdot 34 \\cdot 17^2 \\cdot (\\frac{x^2}{196}+1)\\]\" width=\"274\" height=\"39\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/a/2ea6cf25fc0ce49ded8695f62285432b4910a3ed.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[17x^2=\\frac{25}{2}x^2+2450\\]\" width=\"156\" height=\"37\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/6/f665da9ec4f25d476d5e250dc0e4c6fa4a20e8bb.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x=\\frac{70}{3}\\]\" width=\"54\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p>The perimeter is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b556e33194170ce56b0f241531f21bac27a2d5bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{140}{3}+50=\\frac{290}{3},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"131\" height=\"37\" /> so our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/5/6956da675ee181a23acb94c34c33d8e341b8e6ec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{293}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"39\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<h3><span id=\"Solution_7_.28Similar_to_solution_5.2C_more_in_depth.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_7_(Similar_to_solution_5,_more_in_depth)\">Solution 7 (Similar to solution 5, more in depth)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 7 (Similar to solution 5, more in depth)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let the endpoint of the intersection of the fold near <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/2/6e28ce12d49d39f160d5a0ef54077fc98e4b9d2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$G$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. Since trapezoid <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/8/9182fd187d738b152f8fb896d002b01dbb55571d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BCFE$\" width=\"57\" height=\"12\" /> is folded, it is congruent to trapezoid <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/8/3084d0625bd901d11e3921e0643a1c563403c93a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B&#39;C&#39;FE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"69\" height=\"16\" />. Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/b/43bc8de1003e348404e09c845a75868a68eaa563.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BE=B&#39;E=17$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"132\" height=\"16\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/8/1b844066e5e1579a10c3601c31d89f1767583ec6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle AB&#39;E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"65\" height=\"19\" /> is a right triangle, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/6/32605d9595c86c1647c5428d3d9e350574488a9c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB&#39;=15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"77\" height=\"16\" /> from the pythagorean theorem. From here, we can see that triangles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/b/f1b6a2813e71c5919d6fd5fcfdc94eed5d883cf6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle AEB \\sim \\triangle DGB&#39; \\sim \\triangle C&#39;GF$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"238\" height=\"19\" /> by AA similarity. From here, we find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> from a lot of similarities. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/e/7ce3e753b80409dd0bc8efe53bef3268617483a1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC=x$\" width=\"63\" height=\"12\" />.\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/6/836a5aa422d985cb9cf6fa1d694b4398e576101c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABE&#39; \\sim \\triangle DGB&#39;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"155\" height=\"19\" />:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/d/92de832ff384dcae767c24b5d5b4d8b64ff62830.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac {AE}{AB&#39;} = \\frac{DB}{DG}\\]\" width=\"92\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/2/bd2f00c37fabcd3b36c84c965c19d5d729f20eff.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac {8}{15} = \\frac {x-15}{DG}\\]\" width=\"97\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/3/f13d2f12cdb39330ad995a49756a71bccacdc33b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[DG = \\frac {15(x-15)}{8}\\]\" width=\"139\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/b/dbb26acad0b70ca14972fd95def3a83610156147.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[GF = DC-DG-FC\\]\" width=\"185\" height=\"12\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/e/90e5e78efb53c804f9c86edf9ec8e20545efebb1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[GF = \\frac{-15x+401}{8}\\]\" width=\"146\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/9/7e9f0f5f9006d2b9be2f35ad3933fa9b408ae476.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABE&#39; \\sim \\triangle C&#39;GF&#39;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"158\" height=\"19\" />,\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/1/4f1ca4521706907337aa2dd7ad242cae78c55301.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac {AE}{B&#39;E} = \\frac {C&#39;F}{GF}\\]\" width=\"95\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/a/82a07b29430d3b2df22f45cb6c58cca313496fd9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac {8}{17} = \\frac{3}{\\frac {-15x+401}{8}}\\]\" width=\"112\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p>from which we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/60172e038cfd4c9c324f681cceb9602356c2fd19.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x= \\frac {70}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"59\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p>Finally, our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/2/7228815937763f5b3f94d89ea991bb0cf33d97f2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2(\\frac {70}{3}) + 2(25)=\\frac {290}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"166\" height=\"38\" />, which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/a/acabcf87396fcf61348f4f24b6470822f8ef17b1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$290+3=\\boxed{293}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"123\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p><p>~ Wesserwessey7254\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AIME_II\" title=\"2004 AIME II\">2004 AIME II</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AIME_II_Problems\" title=\"2004 AIME II Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AIME_II_Answer_Key\" title=\"2004 AIME II Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=2004\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2004 AIME II Problems/Problem 6\">Problem 6</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2004 AIME II Problems/Problem 8\">Problem 8</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2004 AIME II Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2004 AIME II Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2004 AIME II Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2004 AIME II Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2004 AIME II Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2004 AIME II Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2004 AIME II Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2004 AIME II Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2004 AIME II Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2004 AIME II Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2004 AIME II Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2004 AIME II Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2004 AIME II Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2004 AIME II Problems/Problem 15\">15</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AIME_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AIME Problems and Solutions\"> All AIME Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017031857\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.075 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.096 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 933/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1806/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 128/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 30867/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   12.463      1 -total\n 59.30%    7.391      1 Template:AIME_box\n 39.00%    4.860      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:2698:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017031857 and revision id 229324. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}